  "tips": "**have dan has = punya**\n\n| Kata ganti | Punya | Contoh |\n|---|---|---|\n| I, you, we, they | **have** | I **have** a brother. |\n| he, she, it | **has** | She **has** two sisters. |\n\nNegatif: **don't have** / **doesn't have** (tidak punya).\nSetelah *doesn't*, kembali ke **have**:\n*She doesn't has a car* ✗ → *She doesn't **have** a car* ✓\n\nKesalahan khas: *I has* ✗, *She have* ✗.\n\nBahasa sehari-hari *Saya ada mobil* (maksudnya punya) tetap memakai **have**: *I have a car.*\n\nPertanyaan: *Do you have a car?* = Apakah kamu punya mobil?\n\nKata baru: **car** = mobil.",
